### Page 1 of 7

```text
MEMORANDUM
TO:

Mayor Patrick Collins, and City Council
FROM:

TJ Barttelbort, Purchasing Manager
DATE:

November 7, 2022
SUBJECT:
Consideration to Purchase between the City of Cheyenne, and Vogel Traffic
Services d/b/a EZ-Liner, for the refurbishment of an existing 2013 EZ-Liner
Striping Truck for the City of Cheyenne Traffic Division
______________________________________________
This is a Sole Source purchase through EZ-Liner, therefore no bids were requested (Sole Source
Letter included).
This request is for the refurbishment of an existing 2013 EZ-Liner Striping Truck, currently in use
by the City of Cheyenne Traffic Division.
From EZ Liner Sole Source Letter:
“EZ Liner is the sole source provider of said striping unit and is fully capable of furnishing all
labor, material, and equipment necessary to recondition or refurbishing the painting equipment
and electronics with new technology to efficiently operate the unit in today’s striping environment.
There is no other company qualified to work on said machine.”
Due to the age of the unit, parts for existing components on the truck are no longer available and
make repairs difficult.  The refurbishment will update parts and components, and bring them to
current production standards.  The paint, bead, and air lines are due for replacement, simply due
to age & usage.  The refurbishment will come with a one (1) year warranty on all new parts.
The total request purchase amount is $157,000.00, for the full refurbishment & rebuild.
Funding:
020-26-2617-42-43102 (1% Sales Tax 19-22 / Equipment)
```

